BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 628.75 Td (since removing one hot item from a tiny pool changes the odds a lot, but real caches are large enough that this) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 615.35 Td (approximation holds well.\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 595.45 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 595.45 Td (Sampling 1 random item: a 1-in-10 chance it's hot. Mistake rate: 10%.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 579.55 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 579.55 Td (Sampling 2 and evicting the older: you only mess up if _both_ picks happen to be hot, since if only one is) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 566.15 Td (hot you'd naturally throw away the cold one instead. First pick: 10% chance of hot. Second pick, from the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 552.75 Td (remaining 999 items with 99 hot ones left: ~=9.9% chance. Multiplied together: 10% \327 9.9% ~= 1%. A 10x) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 539.35 Td (drop from a single extra read.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 523.45 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 523.45 Td (Sampling 3: you'd need all three to be hot: roughly 10% \327 9.9% \327 9.8% ~= 0.1%. Another 10x on paper, but) Tj ET
