BT /F2 14.5 Tf 58.00 547.05 Td (How semantic caching works) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 521.20 Td (Instead of matching queries by exact string, semantic caching matches them by semantic similarity that is by) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 507.80 Td (_meaning_. When a new query comes in, it\222s first converted into an embedding a vector representation of its) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 494.40 Td (meaning. That embedding is then compared against the embeddings already stored in the cache \(cache key\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 481.00 Td (using cosine similarity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 461.10 Td (If the similarity score passes a set threshold \(typically somewhere between 0.85 and 0.95 \(we will see why this) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 447.70 Td (range in particular late in the note\)\), the cache treats the new query as equivalent to a previously seen one. So) Tj ET
