BT /F2 14.5 Tf 58.00 678.75 Td (1. What is CORS ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 652.90 Td (CORS is Cross-Origin Resource Sharing. It is a violation of the Same Origin Policy \(SOP\) of browsers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 633.00 Td (First lets understand what is SOP ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 613.10 Td (Same Origin Policy is a web security mechanism built into web browsers that influences how one website can) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 599.70 Td (access another.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 579.80 Td (Without SOP, another malicious website or web application could access another without restrictions, causing) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 566.40 Td (security vulnerabilitie,s allowing attackers to attack and steal sensitive data or perform actions without user) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 553.00 Td (consent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 533.10 Td (SOP need not be turned on; it automatically comes with browsers. The SOP mechanism was basically built to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 519.70 Td (prevent CSRF\(Cross-Site Request Forgery\) attacks. We will understand about CSRF later.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 499.80 Td (But What is Origin?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 479.90 Td (2 URLs are said to have the same origin if protocol, host and port are the same for both.) Tj ET
