BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 694.75 Td (Let\222s start from Ground Up..) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 674.85 Td (Say we\222re building an app, and as a part of the user registration process we ask users to choose a username. If) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 661.45 Td (the username is already taken, they need to try another one. \(Just like your email, instagram usernames etc..\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 641.55 Td (So as engineers, how should we approach building a feature like this ?) Tj ET
q 479.00 0 0 109.11 58.00 507.54 cm /Im49 Do Q
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 498.54 Td (The most straightforward approach that we can think of is that :) Tj ET
q 479.00 0 0 117.09 58.00 356.56 cm /Im50 Do Q
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 347.56 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 347.56 Td (We will make the UI call an endpoint like this GET /username?q=impraddy) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 331.66 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 331.66 Td (Our backend should check the cache/DB \(SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = \221impraddy\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 315.76 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 315.76 Td (The endpoint should return True/False based on the availability.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 299.86 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 299.86 Td (then make the UI show the feedback instantly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 283.96 Td (This works perfectly\205 at small scale.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 264.06 Td (Now as the app grows, suddenly this endpoint becomes one of our hottest paths because this traditional) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 250.66 Td (approach does a full db scan which takes O\(n\) which is good if the number of rows in our table is limited to some) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 237.26 Td (extent, but at millions and billions of records, the same query will take forever to return the result. \(not only) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 223.86 Td (because we have multiple rows to check, but also that during registration people will retry multiple usernames,) Tj ET
