BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 778.00 Td (so we lose the whole benefit of using it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 758.10 Td (That\222s why sizing matters: we need enough bits \(and the right number of hash functions\) so the filter doesn\222t) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 744.70 Td (get too full, and the false positive rate stays low.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 724.80 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 724.80 Td (_So what do we do when the filter starts getting full? Can we scale it?_) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 708.90 Td (The common approach is to layer Bloom filters \(the idea behind scaling bloom filters\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 689.00 Td (When the current Bloom filter starts getting too full \(too many 1s -> false positives go up\), we don\222t try to expand) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 675.60 Td (the same bit array \(because we would need to rehash and reorder , not optimal\). Instead:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 100.00 655.70 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 108.01 655.70 Td (We freeze the current Bloom filter \(keep it as-is\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 100.00 639.80 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 108.01 639.80 Td (We create a new Bloom filter \(usually bigger / tuned better\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 100.00 623.90 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 108.01 623.90 Td (We insert all new elements into the new one) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 608.00 Td (For query\(element\) operation, you might have to check in all instances of Bloom Filters and then take a decision) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 594.60 Td (accordingly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 574.70 Td (\225) Tj ET
