BT /F2 14.5 Tf 58.00 368.50 Td (Replication) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 342.65 Td (Till now, we have talked about how partitions store data on brokers. But if a partition existed on only one broker,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 329.25 Td (Kafka would not be fault tolerant. If that broker went down, data would be unavailable or even lost. Kafka solves) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 315.85 Td (this using replication.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 295.95 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 295.95 Td (Leader replica: Each partition has one replica elected as the leader, and that leader lives on a broker.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 282.55 Td (Producers and consumers always talk to the leader for that partition.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 266.65 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 266.65 Td (Follower replicas: The same partition is replicated onto other brokers as followers. Followers do not serve) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 253.25 Td (client traffic, they passively replicate data from the leader.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 237.35 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 237.35 Td (Distributed leadership: In the architecture diagram above, notice how leaders are spread across brokers) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 223.95 Td (\(example: Partition A-0 leader on Broker 1, Partition A-1 leader on Broker 2\). This is intentional so read and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 210.55 Td (write load is distributed and no single broker becomes a hotspot.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 194.65 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 194.65 Td (ISR \(In-Sync Replicas\): Followers that are fully caught up with the leader are part of the ISR. ISR is critical) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 181.25 Td (because only an in-sync follower can safely be promoted as the next leader without losing acknowledged) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 167.85 Td (data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 151.95 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 151.95 Td (Failover: If the broker hosting a partition leader goes down, Kafka promotes one of the ISR followers as the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 138.55 Td (new leader, so producers and consumers can continue operating with minimal downtime. When the failed) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 125.15 Td (broker returns, it usually rejoins as a follower and starts replicating again.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 109.25 Td (At this point, we understand what replication is and why Kafka uses leaders, followers, and ISR. But this) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 95.85 Td (naturally raises the next question: who tracks broker liveness, who decides leaders, and who coordinates) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 82.45 Td (failover and metadata updates? That responsibility belongs to Kafka\222s control plane: the KRaft Controller.) Tj ET
