BT /F2 14.5 Tf 58.00 762.00 Td (KRaft Controller) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 736.15 Td (Kafka replication and failover only work if the cluster has a single, consistent authority that coordinates metadata) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 722.75 Td (changes. That role is handled by the Kafka Controller \(Kafka\222s control plane\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 702.85 Td (At a high level, the controller\222s responsibilities include:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 682.95 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 682.95 Td (Leader assignment: deciding which replica is the leader for each partition) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 667.05 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 667.05 Td (Managing replication state: tracking replicas and maintaining the ISR set) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 651.15 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 651.15 Td (Broker health monitoring: detecting when brokers go down or come back up) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 635.25 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 635.25 Td (Failover coordination: when a leader broker fails, promoting an in-sync follower as the new leader so the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 621.85 Td (partition stays available) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 605.95 Td (Earlier versions of Kafka relied on ZooKeeper for this coordination. Modern Kafka replaces ZooKeeper with) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 592.55 Td (KRaft \(Kafka Raft\), where Kafka manages this metadata internally with no external dependency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 572.65 Td (One important note: the controller does not handle data traffic. Producers and consumers do not talk to it) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 559.25 Td (directly. It coordinates the cluster in the background so Kafka keeps working correctly even as brokers come and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 545.85 Td (go.) Tj ET
